      <div type="clause" n="El. 49.8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 49.8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.8" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="46" ed="#liebermann"/>Hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.14"/> ða on monegum senoðum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.15"/> monegra menniscra misdæda bote gesetton, ⁊ on monega senoðbéc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.15"/> hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.6"/> writan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.star3"/>, hwær anne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.16"/> dom hwær oþerne.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.17"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.8" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="46" ed="#liebermann"/>Hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.7"/> ða on monigum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.2"/> synoþu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.9"/></hi> monegra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.11"/> menniscra misdæda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.12"/> bote gesetton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.2"/>, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.2"/> on monegra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.13"/> synoþbec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.7"/> hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.7"/> writon, hwær ænne dóm hwær oþerne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.8" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="47" ed="#liebermann"/>Et in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.1"/> multis synodis suis multorum forisfactorum emendationes aptauerunt et ex multis synodalibus libris undecumque capitula conscripserunt.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.2-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 49.8" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="272" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Hie ða on monegum senoðum monegra menniscra misdæda bote gesetton, ⁊ on monega senoðbéc hie writan, hwær anne dom hwær oþerne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="47" ed="#liebermann"/>Sie setzten da auf vielen Synoden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.1"/> die Busse fest für viele menschliche Missethaten und schrieben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.2"/> sie in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.3"/> viele Synodenbücher<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.4"/>, hier ein Gesetz, dort ein anderes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">They then established at many synods the compensation for many human misdeeds and wrote them into many synod-books, here one law, there another.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="409" ed="#whitelock"/>They then in many synods fixed the compensations for many human misdeeds, and they wrote them in many synod-books, here one law, there another.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="273" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Then they established in many synods the remedies for the various misdeeds of men, and they wrote in many books of synodal decrees, in one place one judgment and in one place another.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hi <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hi So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seon. <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seon. So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">writon <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> awritan hetton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">writon So; awritan hetton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ænne <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ænne So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nächste Zeile leer E</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">next line blank E</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> manega</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to manega</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gra <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur;</hi> o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gra on an erasure; o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">47</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scrips. <hi rend="italic">Hk. Schmid nimmt hier folgende Zeilen auf:</hi> Ista et decem Dei precepta et leges Mosaicas et iudicia quæ ipse Deus locutus est ad Moysen et præcepit ei custodire Elfredus rex Westsaxonum simul fecit colligi et in scriptis redigi, ita dicens: <hi rend="italic">sie stehen nur in Bromton und gehören nicht zum Quadripartitus</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scrips. Hk. Schmid includes the following lines here: Ista et decem Dei precepta et leges Mosaicas et iudicia quæ ipse Deus locutus est ad Moysen et præcepit ei custodire Elfredus rex Westsaxonum simul fecit colligi et in scriptis redigi, ita dicens: they occur only in Bromton and do not belong to the Quadripartitus</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">49</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> 49, 7².</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 49, 7².</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">49</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘liessen niederschreiben’ Ld aus verlorener Hs., zwar genauer, da die Witan nicht selbst Schreibarbeit taten, aber nicht authentisch und vielleicht aus 49, 9 Z. 2 vorweggenommen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘had [them] written down’ Ld from a lost MS — more precise, it is true, since the Witan did not do the writing themselves, but not authentic, and perhaps anticipated from 49, 9 l. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">49</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘aus, gemäss, nach’ Q, falsch laut des folgenden ‘hier — dort’, was Q folgerichtig zu ‘überall <hi rend="spaced">her</hi>’ verdrehen muss. Synodaldekrete als geistige Quelle auch weltlicher Gesetzgebung 7. — 9. Jhs. hinzustellen, schmeichelt Q’s Klerikalismus. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> S. 34 Z. 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘from, according to, after’ Q, wrong in view of the following ‘here — there’, which Q consequently has to twist into ‘from <hi rend="italic">everywhere</hi>’. To present synodal decrees as the intellectual source even of the secular legislation of the 7th–9th cent. flatters Q’s clericalism. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> p. 34 l. 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-49-8.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Witenagemot-Bücher sind unbekannt. Auch meint Af keine <hi rend="italic">domboc</hi> bürgerlichen Rechts, sondern Zerstreuung der Gesetze durch Bücher hin, die auch anderes enthielten, und zwar, da er sie Synodbücher nennt, Konzilien, vermutlich neben anderer kanonistischer Literatur. Nur so sind uns die meisten Agsä. Gesetze erhalten, auch Abt und Af. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Archiv 2; Gesetz 3d</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Books of the witenagemot are unknown. Nor does Af mean a <hi rend="italic">domboc</hi> of civil law, but rather the dispersal of the laws through books that contained other matter as well — namely, since he calls them synod-books, councils, presumably alongside other canonistic literature. It is only in this way that most Anglo-Saxon laws have come down to us, Abt and Af among them. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Archiv 2; Gesetz 3d</seg></note>
      </div>
